<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17596" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">falcĭfer</span></b> , ĕra,
			ĕrum, adj.
		falx + fero, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>sickle-bearing</i>, <i>holding a
				scythe</i> or <i>sickle.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">covinus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					17, 418</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">manus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 13, 930</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic., <i>an epithet of Saturn</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">senex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. Ib.
					218</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tonans,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					5, 16, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
